Package: RegCompassR
Title: Multiome Regulatory Evidence and Metabolic Reaction Analysis
Version: 2.2.4
Authors@R: c(person(given = "RegCompass", family = "Developers", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "dev@example.com"))
Author: RegCompass Developers [aut, cre]
Maintainer: RegCompass Developers <dev@example.com>
Description: Integrates paired single-cell RNA and ATAC regulatory evidence
    with genome-scale metabolic reaction analysis. When two or more condition
    levels are available, RegCompass fits one condition-aware Pando design per
    broad cell type and uses condition-full outer-heldout TF-by-ATAC projections
    as the primary regulatory penalty. Jointly estimable edges form an auditable
    common-support component; edges non-estimable in one or both conditions
    contribute projectable structural zeros in those conditions. A supplied
    single-level condition directly uses original Pando infer_grn with unscaled
    predictors and no condition coefficients; an explicitly missing condition
    column is rejected. Condition-aware runs require the registered Pando >= 1.5.1
    C++ product and multitask kernels and stop immediately if native registration
    or execution is unavailable. Metacells use one independent multimodal WNN
    graph per broad cell type through SuperCell SCimplify_by_graph_group. All
    conditions within a cell type jointly determine adaptive RNA and ATAC
    modality weights, neighbours, and Walktrap clusters; condition splits the
    parent memberships only after clustering. Metacell RNA and ATAC counts use
    exact SuperCell membership. Small metacells are retained and marked rather
    than merged or removed. RNA latent expression uses normalized-unit empirical
    Bayes updates whose shrinkage weights are independent of library size;
    observed zeros retain continuous posterior evidence and are not
    threshold-clamped. Regulatory modifiers act on bounded RNA-support odds,
    GPR rules produce reaction expression, and each medium uses one shared union
    GEM and global FASTCORE completion. Directional structural vmax is solved
    once per shared model and target, then reused across metacells. Built-in
    medium scenarios are restricted to formulations with direct published-paper
    provenance. Depth matching, common-depth restriction, alpha sensitivity,
    zero-support sensitivity and link-saturation propagation are not part of the
    canonical workflow.
